= *Viet-Hoang Tran*






I'm currently a fourth-year Ph.D. student in the [https://www.math.nus.edu.sg/ Department of Mathematics], [https://nus.edu.sg/ National University of Singapore].

\n

\n

I began my Ph.D. in August 2022 in Mathematics. In September 2023, I shifted my research focus to Machine Learning and started working under the supervision of Professor [https://tanmnguyen89.github.io/ Tan Minh Nguyen].

\n

\n

Previously, I completed an Honors degree in Mathematics at the [https://english.hus.vnu.edu.vn/ Hanoi University of Science] (2018-2022). \n

\n

email: hoang.tranviet \[at\] u.nus.edu {{<span style="margin-left:15px;"></span> }} | {{<span style="margin-left:15px;"></span> }} [https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=HXsV5dQAAAAJ&view_op=list_works&sortby=pubdate Google Scholar] 








== *Research Interests*

- My research focuses on symmetries in neural networks: understanding how distinct parameter configurations can represent the same function and characterizing the relationships between them. I am also interested in applications of these symmetries, including equivariant metanetworks, neural conservation laws, linear mode connectivity up to symmetry, and model merging.

- I am also interested in AI-assisted mathematical reasoning and theorem proving, and, more broadly, in understanding the reasoning capabilities and limitations of LLMs.

{{}}

keywords: machine learning, parameter space symmetry, mode connectivity, neural conservation law, metanetwork







== *News*

- *Aug 2026*. Amid the Math-AI hype, with help from GPT-5.6 Sol, Claude Fable 5, and our agentic harness built around these models, we explored several open problems and obtained the following results. All three papers are preprints and have not yet been peer reviewed:
-- *The Noetherian case of Bayart's power-series question.* If {{<i>R</i>}} is a commutative Noetherian ring and {{<i>R</i>[[<i>x</i>]]}} is a UFD, then {{<i>R</i>[[<i>x</i>,<i>y</i>]]}} is also a UFD. Preprint available [https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.12642 here]. The question for arbitrary domains, without the Noetherian assumption, remains open.
-- *Polynomial extensions of SFT rings.* Must {{<i>R</i>[<i>x</i>]}} be SFT whenever {{<i>R</i>}} is a commutative SFT ring? Positive results were known under additional hypotheses; we answer the general question negatively by constructing a one-dimensional local SFT domain {{<i>R</i>}} for which {{<i>R</i>[<i>x</i>]}} is not SFT. Preprint available [https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.26044 here].
-- *A new six-vertex Erdős-Hajnal case.* Up to isomorphism, the 26 prime graphs on six vertices form 13 complementary pairs. Four pairs were previously known to have the Erdős-Hajnal property---two through published or accepted results and two through a preprint. We establish a fifth pair by proving the property for the graph with edge set \{ab,bc,cd,de,af,bf,df\}. Preprint available [https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.28551 here].

- *May 2026*. 3 papers accepted at ICML 2026:
-- [https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.17816 *Conservation Laws for Modern Neural Architectures*] *(spotlight)*
-- [https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.17830 *Functional Equivalence in Attention: A Comprehensive Study with Applications to Linear Mode Connectivity*]
-- [https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.19036 *Geometric and Stochastic Analysis of Discontinuities in Sparse Mixture-of-Experts*] *(spotlight)*

- *Jan 2026*. 4 papers accepted at ICLR 2026:
-- [https://openreview.net/forum?id=XMiDpi2mWY *Quasi-Equivariant Metanetworks*]
-- [https://openreview.net/forum?id=e439wJl5sT *Mixed-Curvature Tree-Sliced Wasserstein Distance*]
-- [https://openreview.net/forum?id=HHNQSXaLkF *Tree-sliced Sobolev IPM*]
-- [https://openreview.net/forum?id=kDqG03v05B *Revisiting Tree-Sliced Wasserstein Distance Through the Lens of the Fermat-Weber Problem*]

